{
 "id": "caro-kann",
 "name": "Caro-Kann Defence",
 "kind": "opening",
 "track": "openings",
 "level": "beginner",
 "goal": "As Black against 1.e4, you can play the Caro-Kann: support d5 with the c-pawn on c6, bring out the bishop on c8 early, and keep a solid position.",
 "priorKnowledge": [
  "opening-principles"
 ],
 "side": "black",
 "eco": "B19",
 "puzzleTags": [
  "Caro-Kann_Defense"
 ],
 "puzzleThemes": [],
 "intro": {
  "text": "The Caro-Kann answers 1.e4, White's pawn to e4, with 1...c6, your c-pawn one step forward, and then ...d5. The c-pawn backs up the d-pawn, so you keep a firm share of the centre. Unlike 1...e6, which shuts the bishop on c8 in behind a pawn, it leaves that bishop a clear road out as soon as the d-pawn has moved, and the bishop comes out early. You get a solid position with few weak points for White to attack."
 },
