   "side": "black",
   "keyIdea": "Support your centre pawn with the c-pawn, and bring the light-squared bishop out before your e-pawn shuts it in.",
   "text": "You are Black, and White opens with 1.e4. The moves you will play are known as the Classical Variation. At each move, ask what it does for your centre and your pieces, and what White is threatening.",
