      "text": "1...c6 looks modest, but it is there to support ...d5: if White ever takes a pawn on d5, your c-pawn can take back. Your e-pawn stays at home, so as soon as your d-pawn moves to d5, the bishop on c8, the one that moves on light squares, has an open diagonal and can come out early."
